===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:cler|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|clere}}, from {{der|en|xno|cler}}, from {{der|en|fro|cler}} (Modern {{cog|fr|clair}}), from {{der|en|la|clarus}}. Displaced native [[Middle English]] {{m|enm|schir||clear, pure}} (from [[Old English]] {{m|ang|scīr||clear, bright}}), [[Middle English]] {{m|enm|skere||clear, sheer}} (from [[Old English]] {{m|ang|scǣre}} and Old Norse {{m|non|skær|skǣr|sheer, clear, pure}}), [[Middle English]] {{m|enm|smolt||clear (of mind), serene}} (from [[Old English]] {{m|ang|smolt||peaceful, serene}}).  Cognate with {{cog|da,de,nb,nn,sv|klar}}, {{cog|nl|klaar}}, {{cog|fr|clair}}, {{cog|it|chiaro}}, {{cog|pt|claro}}, {{cog|ro|clar}}, {{cog|es|claro}}.

